# Introduction

Thanks for considering contributing to this project!

Any contribution is encouraged and welcome.

## Ground Rules

There is one ground rule for contributions:

> Your contribution will need to use the same license as this project in order to be accepted.

## How to Contribute

All contributions should be submitted via a Pull Request. Never done a pull request before? [See this tutorial!](http://makeapullrequest.com/).

See [Development]({% if zensical_ghpages %}{{ docs_url }}maintaining/development/{% else %}docs/maintaining/development.md{% endif %}) for setting up your workstation and the commit and PR title conventions.

If your contribution is accepted, you will be added to the Contributors section in the README.

## How to report a bug

### Vulnerabilities

If you find a security vulnerability, please do NOT open an Issue. Instead, choose **Security Vulnerability** when opening a new issue (or use the vulnerability reporting feature on the Security tab) to report it privately.

### Non-Security Bugs

For non-security bugs, please open a new issue and choose the **Bug Report** template.

## How to suggest a feature or enhancement

If you wish to suggest a feature or enhancement, please open a new issue and choose the **Feature Request** template.

## Code review process

The owners of this project will conduct code reviews on a best-effort basis.

## Questions

If you have additional questions about contributing, please open a new issue and choose the **Question** template.
